lding and favour seeking. That the priestly elite maintained some autonomy and influence was best illustrated during royal succession struggles, when shrine heads sometimes accepted the risks involved in partisanship." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 857, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 764})
